  <p>
    Hardcover Foundation is recognized by the Internal Revenue Service as
    exempt from federal income tax under Section 501(c)(3) and is classified
    as a public charity under Section 170(b)(1)(A)(vi). Its federal tax
    exemption is effective July 6, 2025.
  </p>

  <h2>Corporate Facts</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Hardcover Foundation is a Virginia nonstock corporation.</li>
    <li>The corporation has no statutory members.</li>
    <li>
      Its Virginia Certificate of Restatement is effective September 17,
      2025.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Charitable and Educational Purposes</h2>
  <p>Hardcover Foundation's governing documents identify purposes that include:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      preserving and elevating cultural and literary heritage through
      literacy, storytelling, mentorship, and creative programming
    </li>
    <li>
      empowering youth and communities through educational workshops,
      cultural partnerships, and creative initiatives
    </li>
    <li>
      collaborating with nonprofit organizations for educational and
      community enrichment
    </li>
  </ul>

